# GeoSense - the ONE place for site-specific SLURM values.
#
#   cp scripts/slurm/cluster.env.example scripts/slurm/cluster.env     # cluster.env is git-ignored
#
# Every value below is a PLACEHOLDER until checked against the output of
#   bash scripts/slurm/00_inspect_cluster.sh
# (the [section] names in the comments refer to that output). This file is plain bash: it is
# `source`d by the scripts, so keep the KEY="value" form and no spaces around `=`.
# Never put a password, token or Kaggle key in this file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SLURM resources (submit.sh turns them into sbatch options; an EMPTY value is simply not passed)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# GPU partition. [sinfo]: a partition whose GRES column shows gpu:... and whose AVAIL is "up".
# Empty = the cluster's default partition (marked with * in sinfo).
GS_PARTITION=""

# Account to charge. [sacctmgr assoc]: the "Account" column for your user. Empty = your default.
GS_ACCOUNT=""

# Quality of service. [sacctmgr assoc]: "QOS" / "Def QOS" columns; [sacctmgr qos] shows each
# QOS's MaxWall. Empty = your default QOS.
GS_QOS=""

# GPU request. [sinfo GRES per partition]: if GRES shows gpu:a100:4 you may write "gpu:a100:1"
# to ask for that type, or "gpu:1" for any GPU. One GPU is enough (the code uses a single GPU).
GS_GRES="gpu:1"

# Wall-time of a training job, HH:MM:SS (or D-HH:MM:SS). Must be <= the partition TIMELIMIT
# ([sinfo] / [scontrol show partition] MaxTime) and the QOS MaxWall. A job cut by the limit is
# not lost: re-submit it, --resume continues from the last finished epoch.
GS_TIME="08:00:00"

# Wall-time of the smoke test and of the export job. Raise GS_SMOKE_TIME to 00:30:00 if the
# smoke job is killed by the limit on a slow GPU.
GS_SMOKE_TIME="00:15:00"
GS_EXPORT_TIME="01:00:00"

# CPU cores (DataLoader workers = cores - 1) and RAM per job. [sinfo]: CPUS and MEMORY (MB) per
# node; ask for a fraction of a node proportional to the GPUs you use (1 of 4 GPUs -> ~1/4).
GS_CPUS="8"
GS_MEM="48G"

# Extra sbatch options as a bash array, e.g. (--constraint=a100) or (--exclude=node12).
GS_EXTRA_SBATCH_ARGS=()

# 1 = add `--requeue --signal=B:USR1@120`: SLURM warns the job 2 minutes before the time limit and
# the job puts itself back in the queue, then resumes from last.pt. 0 = re-submit by hand
# (the required mechanism; always works). Only use 1 if one epoch is shorter than GS_TIME,
# otherwise the job is requeued forever without progress.
GS_AUTO_REQUEUE="0"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Software
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Modules to load before anything else, space-separated. [module avail]: pick a conda/anaconda/
# miniforge module (if conda is not already on your PATH, see [python / conda]). A CUDA module is
# NOT needed: the pip PyTorch wheels ship their own CUDA libraries. Example: "anaconda3/2024.02".
GS_MODULES=""

# Only if `conda` is not on the PATH even after the modules: path to conda.sh of a personal
# Miniforge install, e.g. "$HOME/miniforge3/etc/profile.d/conda.sh". Otherwise leave empty.
GS_CONDA_SH=""

# auto = conda if available, else a Python venv. Force with "conda" or "venv".
GS_ENV_KIND="auto"

# Conda env: a NAME (lives in ~/.conda or the conda install) or a PATH (e.g. on a project
# disk when the $HOME quota is small - the env needs ~6 GB, see [disk]).
GS_CONDA_ENV="geosense"

# venv fallback location (used only when there is no conda). Needs python >= 3.10.
GS_VENV_DIR="$HOME/venvs/geosense"

# Optional: a specific PyTorch CUDA build. Leave empty to use the default PyPI wheel. If the
# driver is old ([nvidia-smi] "CUDA Version" < 12), use e.g. https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu118
GS_TORCH_INDEX_URL=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paths (absolute; quotes matter if a path has spaces)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The clone of this repo on the cluster. Empty = the repo that contains this file.
GEOSENSE_REPO=""

# The Kaggle `compressed_dataset` folder (one sub-folder per country, 49,997 JPEGs, 6.7 GB).
# fetch_assets.sh downloads into its parent. Choose a disk with >= 15 GB free ([disk]); fast
# storage (scratch/project) is better than $HOME for 33k image reads per epoch.
GEOSENSE_DATA="/scratch/$USER/geosense/compressed_dataset"

# Checkpoints (last.pt / best.pt per run, a few hundred MB per run): scratch, never the repo.
# Check [disk] for the scratch path ($SCRATCH, /scratch/$USER, ...) and whether it is purged.
GEOSENSE_CKPT="/scratch/$USER/geosense/checkpoints"

# Hugging Face cache: StreetCLIP is downloaded here once (1.7 GB) by fetch_assets.sh, then the
# jobs read it with HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 (compute nodes often have no internet).
HF_HOME="/scratch/$USER/geosense/hf_home"
